- Add a script arkoor genesis transition
  An arkoor transaction can now spend a VTXO through a tapscript leaf that
  the client cosigners and the Ark server cosign. Validation does not need
  the VTXO policy of the spent output, so wallets can validate spends of
  policies that they do not know.
  [#2883](https://gitlab.com/ark-bitcoin/bark/-/merge_requests/2883)
  - **BREAKING:** `TransitionKind` has a new `ScriptArkoor` variant.
- Make the user pubkey of a VTXO optional
  This prepares for VTXO policies that have no single user key, like an
  HTLC between two users.
  [#2883](https://gitlab.com/ark-bitcoin/bark/-/merge_requests/2883)
  - **BREAKING:** `Vtxo::user_pubkey` and `VtxoPolicy::user_pubkey` now
    return `Option<PublicKey>`.
  - **BREAKING:** The attestation `verify` methods now return
    `AttestationVerifyError` instead of `secp256k1::Error`.
  - **BREAKING:** `VtxoTreeSpec::new` now returns
    `Result<VtxoTreeSpec, NoUserPubkeyError>`. It fails if a leaf policy
    has no user pubkey.
